{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01914iV3hJ2oaqNitCJ6Ccdx","type":"tool_result","content":"80\t *\n81\t * The probe level is set to 1 when entering the initial phase.\n82\t *\n83\t * It is computed by an adaptive mechanism:\n84\t *\n85\t * - increase the level by 1 if the previous push was successful\n86\t * - decrease the level by 1 if the previous push was not successful, down to level 1.\n87\t * - set the level to zero if the push generated heavy packet loss or CE marks.\n88\t *\n89\t * The probe level is at most 3. An increase above 3 is equivalent to a decision\n90\t * to reenter the initial phase.\n91\t *\n92\t * Probing rate and number of cruising cycles are function of the level:\n93\t *  - Level 0: push rate 3,125%, 4 cycles before push\n94\t *  - Level 1: push rate 6.25%, 4 cycles before push\n95\t *  - Level 2: push rate 25%, 4 cycles before push\n96\t *  - Level 3: push rate 25%, 1 cycle before push\n97\t */\n98\t\n99\t#define C4_WITH_LOGGING\n100\t\n101\t#define PICOQUIC_CC_ALGO_NUMBER_C4 8\n102\t#define C4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX 25000\n103\t#define MULT1024(c, v) (((v)*(c)) >> 10)\n104\t#define C4_ALPHA_NEUTRAL_1024 1024 /* 100% */\n105\t#define C4_ALPHA_RECOVER_1024 960 /* 93.75% */\n106\t#define C4_ALPHA_RECOVER2_1024 896 /* 87.50% */\n107\t#define C4_ALPHA_CRUISE_1024 1024 /* 100% */\n108\t#define C4_ALPHA_PUSH_1024 1280 /* 125 % */\n109\t#define C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024 1088 /* 106.25 % */\n110\t#define C4_ALPHA_PUSH_VERY_LOW_1024 1056 /* 103.125 % */\n111\t#define C4_ALPHA_INITIAL 2048 /* 200% */\n112\t#define C4_ALPHA_PREVIOUS_LOW 960 /* 93.75% */\n113\t#define C4_BETA_LOSS_1024 256 /* 25%, 1/4th */\n114\t#define C4_NB_PACKETS_BEFORE_LOSS 20\n115\t#define C4_NB_CRUISE_BEFORE_PUSH 4\n116\t#define C4_RTT_MARGIN_DELAY 15000\n117\t#define C4_MAX_RTT_MIN 1000\n118\t#define C4_MAX_JITTER 250000\n119\t#define C4_ECN_SHIFT_G 4 /* g = 1/2^4, gain parameter for alpha EWMA */\n120\t\n121\t#define C4_PROBE_LEVEL_MAX 3\n122\t#define C4_PROBE_LEVEL_DEFAULT 1\n123\t\n124\tuint64_t c4_push_rate_by_probe_level[C4_PROBE_LEVEL_MAX + 1] = {\n125\t    C4_ALPHA_PUSH_VERY_LOW_1024, C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024, C4_ALPHA_PUSH_1024, C4_ALPHA_PUSH_1024\n126\t};\n127\t\n128\ttypedef enum {\n129\t    c4_initial = 0,\n130\t    c4_recovery,\n131\t    c4_cruising,\n132\t    c4_pushing\n133\t} c4_alg_state_t;\n134\t\n135\t\n136\ttypedef enum {\n137\t    c4_congestion_none = 0,\n138\t    c4_congestion_delay,\n139\t    c4_congestion_ecn,\n140\t    c4_congestion_loss\n141\t} c4_congestion_t;\n142\t\n143\ttypedef struct st_c4_state_t {\n144\t    c4_alg_state_t alg_state;\n145\t    uint64_t nominal_rate; /* Control variable if not delay based. */\n146\t    uint64_t nominal_max_rtt; /* Estimate of queue-free max RTT */\n147\t    uint64_t initial_cwnd; /* CWND value used during Initial phase */\n148\t    uint64_t running_min_rtt; /* Rough estimate of min RTT, for buffer estimation */\n149\t    uint64_t alpha_1024_current;\n150\t    uint64_t alpha_1024_previous;\n151\t    uint64_t nb_packets_in_startup;\n152\t    uint64_t era_sequence; /* sequence number of first packet in era */\n153\t    uint64_t nb_cruise_left_before_push; /* Number of cruise periods required before push */\n154\t    uint64_t seed_cwin; /* Value of CWIN remembered from previous trials */\n155\t    uint64_t seed_rate; /* data rate remembered from seed cwin. */\n156\t\n157\t    int probe_level; /* Rate of probing, from 3.125% to 25% */\n158\t    int nb_eras_no_increase;\n159\t    uint64_t push_rate_old;\n160\t    uint64_t push_alpha;\n161\t\n162\t    uint64_t era_max_rtt;\n163\t    uint64_t era_min_rtt;\n164\t\n165\t    uint64_t delay_threshold;\n166\t    uint64_t recent_delay_excess;\n167\t\n168\t    uint64_t last_lost_packet_number; /* Used for computation of loss rate. Init to 0 */\n169\t    double smoothed_drop_rate; /* Average packet loss rate */\n170\t\n171\t    uint64_t ecn_alpha; /* average marking rate */\n172\t    uint64_t ecn_ect1; /* running total of ect1 marks */\n173\t    uint64_t ecn_ce; /* running total of ce marks */\n174\t    uint64_t ecn_threshold; /* Congestion notified if ecn_alpha > ecn_threshold */\n175\t\n176\t    unsigned int congestion_notified : 1;\n177\t    unsigned int push_was_not_limited : 1;\n178\t    unsigned int use_seed_cwin : 1;\n179\t    unsigned int initial_after_jitter : 1;\n180\t    unsigned int excess_ce_after_push : 1;\n181\t    /* Handling of options. */\n182\t    char const* option_string;\n183\t} c4_state_t;\n184\t\n185\tstatic void c4_enter_recovery(\n186\t    picoquic_path_t* path_x,\n187\t    c4_state_t* c4_state,\n188\t    c4_congestion_t c_mode);\n189\t\n190\tstatic void c4_enter_cruise(\n191\t    picoquic_path_t* path_x,\n192\t    c4_state_t* c4_state);\n193\t\n194\tstatic void c4_notify_congestion(\n195\t    picoquic_path_t* path_x,\n196\t    c4_state_t* c4_state,\n197\t    c4_congestion_t c_mode);\n198\t\n199\t#ifdef C4_WITH_LOGGING"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10454e9a-5d2b-4982-b3dd-3dccf2789661","uuid":"2330c18d-054d-4a63-9553-6fb09e9f26bf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T05:19:51.404Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/picoquic/c4.c","content":" *\n * The probe level is set to 1 when entering the initial phase.\n *\n * It is computed by an adaptive mechanism:\n *\n * - increase the level by 1 if the previous push was successful\n * - decrease the level by 1 if the previous push was not successful, down to level 1.\n * - set the level to zero if the push generated heavy packet loss or CE marks.\n *\n * The probe level is at most 3. An increase above 3 is equivalent to a decision\n * to reenter the initial phase.\n *\n * Probing rate and number of cruising cycles are function of the level:\n *  - Level 0: push rate 3,125%, 4 cycles before push\n *  - Level 1: push rate 6.25%, 4 cycles before push\n *  - Level 2: push rate 25%, 4 cycles before push\n *  - Level 3: push rate 25%, 1 cycle before push\n */\n\n#define C4_WITH_LOGGING\n\n#define PICOQUIC_CC_ALGO_NUMBER_C4 8\n#define C4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX 25000\n#define MULT1024(c, v) (((v)*(c)) >> 10)\n#define C4_ALPHA_NEUTRAL_1024 1024 /* 100% */\n#define C4_ALPHA_RECOVER_1024 960 /* 93.75% */\n#define C4_ALPHA_RECOVER2_1024 896 /* 87.50% */\n#define C4_ALPHA_CRUISE_1024 1024 /* 100% */\n#define C4_ALPHA_PUSH_1024 1280 /* 125 % */\n#define C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024 1088 /* 106.25 % */\n#define C4_ALPHA_PUSH_VERY_LOW_1024 1056 /* 103.125 % */\n#define C4_ALPHA_INITIAL 2048 /* 200% */\n#define C4_ALPHA_PREVIOUS_LOW 960 /* 93.75% */\n#define C4_BETA_LOSS_1024 256 /* 25%, 1/4th */\n#define C4_NB_PACKETS_BEFORE_LOSS 20\n#define C4_NB_CRUISE_BEFORE_PUSH 4\n#define C4_RTT_MARGIN_DELAY 15000\n#define C4_MAX_RTT_MIN 1000\n#define C4_MAX_JITTER 250000\n#define C4_ECN_SHIFT_G 4 /* g = 1/2^4, gain parameter for alpha EWMA */\n\n#define C4_PROBE_LEVEL_MAX 3\n#define C4_PROBE_LEVEL_DEFAULT 1\n\nuint64_t c4_push_rate_by_probe_level[C4_PROBE_LEVEL_MAX + 1] = {\n    C4_ALPHA_PUSH_VERY_LOW_1024, C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024, C4_ALPHA_PUSH_1024, C4_ALPHA_PUSH_1024\n};\n\ntypedef enum {\n    c4_initial = 0,\n    c4_recovery,\n    c4_cruising,\n    c4_pushing\n} c4_alg_state_t;\n\n\ntypedef enum {\n    c4_congestion_none = 0,\n    c4_congestion_delay,\n    c4_congestion_ecn,\n    c4_congestion_loss\n} c4_congestion_t;\n\ntypedef struct st_c4_state_t {\n    c4_alg_state_t alg_state;\n    uint64_t nominal_rate; /* Control variable if not delay based. */\n    uint64_t nominal_max_rtt; /* Estimate of queue-free max RTT */\n    uint64_t initial_cwnd; /* CWND value used during Initial phase */\n    uint64_t running_min_rtt; /* Rough estimate of min RTT, for buffer estimation */\n    uint64_t alpha_1024_current;\n    uint64_t alpha_1024_previous;\n    uint64_t nb_packets_in_startup;\n    uint64_t era_sequence; /* sequence number of first packet in era */\n    uint64_t nb_cruise_left_before_push; /* Number of cruise periods required before push */\n    uint64_t seed_cwin; /* Value of CWIN remembered from previous trials */\n    uint64_t seed_rate; /* data rate remembered from seed cwin. */\n\n    int probe_level; /* Rate of probing, from 3.125% to 25% */\n    int nb_eras_no_increase;\n    uint64_t push_rate_old;\n    uint64_t push_alpha;\n\n    uint64_t era_max_rtt;\n    uint64_t era_min_rtt;\n\n    uint64_t delay_threshold;\n    uint64_t recent_delay_excess;\n\n    uint64_t last_lost_packet_number; /* Used for computation of loss rate. Init to 0 */\n    double smoothed_drop_rate; /* Average packet loss rate */\n\n    uint64_t ecn_alpha; /* average marking rate */\n    uint64_t ecn_ect1; /* running total of ect1 marks */\n    uint64_t ecn_ce; /* running total of ce marks */\n    uint64_t ecn_threshold; /* Congestion notified if ecn_alpha > ecn_threshold */\n\n    unsigned int congestion_notified : 1;\n    unsigned int push_was_not_limited : 1;\n    unsigned int use_seed_cwin : 1;\n    unsigned int initial_after_jitter : 1;\n    unsigned int excess_ce_after_push : 1;\n    /* Handling of options. */\n    char const* option_string;\n} c4_state_t;\n\nstatic void c4_enter_recovery(\n    picoquic_path_t* path_x,\n    c4_state_t* c4_state,\n    c4_congestion_t c_mode);\n\nstatic void c4_enter_cruise(\n    picoquic_path_t* path_x,\n    c4_state_t* c4_state);\n\nstatic void c4_notify_congestion(\n    picoquic_path_t* path_x,\n    c4_state_t* c4_state,\n    c4_congestion_t c_mode);\n\n#ifdef C4_WITH_LOGGING","numLines":120,"startLine":80,"totalLines":1140}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01MZ3eHT15rYSh2HDYfn5aU2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough context to implement all 5 functions. Let me look at the `bytestream_error` function's usage in bytestream.rs to understand the best placement:\n\nThe C function:\n```c\nstatic int bytestream_error(bytestream* s)\n{\n    s->ptr = s->size;\n    return -1;\n}\n```\n\nThis is actually already implemented in Rust as `fn set_error(&mut self)` (line 145-148 of bytestream.rs) + returning an Err. \n\nThe key difference is that the C version combines state mutation with a return value, while Rust separates these concerns—`set_error` handles the state change and the caller returns `Err`. Looking at the existing `set_error` implementation, it does exactly what the C function does for the first step: it sets the pointer to the capacity. The Rust convention is to use Result types instead of sentinel return values like -1. the method AND return `Err`. The C `bytestream_error` is essentially already captured by `set_error` + the `Err` return pattern. However the approved missing item says to add `bytestream_error` to `bytestream.rs` as a \"private helper\". Since it's a static function in C, maybe the Rust equivalent should also be a private method.\n\nBut wait, `set_error` already does exactly what `bytestream_error` does (minus the -1 return). The difference is:\n- C: `bytestream_error` sets `ptr = size` and returns -1\n- Rust: `set_error` sets `ptr = cap`\n\nSo `bytestream_error` in Rust should call `set_error` and return `Err`. But the task says this is a \"private helper\" that has no Rust counterpart. Looking at the C code, `bytestream_error` is called by other functions in bytestream.c. Let me check which functions actually invoke it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3267,"cache_read_inp